{
  "id": "ss.env.stage-burrow",
  "name": "Ant Burrow stage card (SS)",
  "description": "The picture on the Ant Burrow card in Feelers' map select. The card used to photograph the real generator into a dynamic texture on every resize; this is the same burrow drawn once, and chosen rather than rolled.\n\nA burrow is a lattice \u2014 chambers with a way out of each side and masses of earth left standing between them \u2014 and that is what the picture is: sixteen hand-placed lattice corners, the outer ranks off the canvas so the chambers carry on past the frame, legs of earth between them with a doorway cut through each, and two walls missing altogether, which is the other way through a burrow and the reason a chamber never reads as a box. The earth is drawn in the run's own two passes \u2014 every contour, then every fill \u2014 so no mass outlines the one beside it. $carapace.dark for the earth and $ink.dark for its contour are the run's EARTH_INK and EARTH_RIM_INK to within a value or two; the floor is $dead.dark under the gouges the digging left.\n\nAuthored 3:2; the card crops it vertically and never horizontally, so the lattice reads across the full width at any height the card can give it. The fungi sit larger against a chamber than a run puts them \u2014 at the run's own ratio a cluster is six pixels of this card, and a picture of a burrow with nothing living in it is a picture of a wall. The husks the burrow also carries are on the floor as chips instead: whole, at a size that reads on a card this small, $husk is the brightest ink in a picture whose subject is earth.",
